The obtained NN potential is applicable to simulations of crystalline and amorphous bulk structures, clusters, and slabs. The accuracy for these structure types has been checked by investigating a wide range of systems. In Fig. 2 the energy vs volume curves for several crystal structures of ZnO are shown. As in DFT and experiment, the wurtzite structure is found to be energetically most stable and even the tiny energy difference to the zinc blende structure is correctly resolved. It can be seen that the potential is also valid for compressed structures, as the smallest investigated volumes in Fig. 2 correspond to pressures of about 70 GPa . The obtained lattice parameters and cohesive energies of the investigated phases are given in Table I. The NN and DFT energies of 40 random bulk structures containing 4 zinc and 4 oxygen atoms are shown in Fig. 3. These structures, which have not been included in the training set,

